    "problemStatement": "You are given NNN sets of integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. For each valid iii, let's denote the elements of the set AiA_iAi​ by {ci,1,ci,2,…,ci,∣Ai∣}\\{c_{i,1}, c_{i,2}, \\ldots, c_{i,|A_i|}\\}{ci,1​,ci,2​,…,ci,∣Ai​∣​}.\n\nFind the number of ways to choose a sequence (a1,a2,…,aN)(a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_N)(a1​,a2​,…,aN​) such that:\n\n\nai∈Aia_i \\in A_iai​∈Ai​ for each valid iii\nai≠ai+1a_i \\neq a_{i+1}ai​=ai+1​ for each valid iii and a1≠aNa_1 \\neq a_Na1​=aN​\nSince this number may be large, compute it modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
    "constraints": [
      "2≤N≤200,0002 \\le N \\le 200,0002≤N≤200,000",
      "∣Ai∣≥1|A_i| \\ge 1∣Ai​∣≥1 for each valid iii",
      "∣A1∣+∣A2∣+…+∣AN∣≤200,000|A_1| + |A_2| + \\ldots + |A_N| \\le 200,000∣A1​∣+∣A2​∣+…+∣AN​∣≤200,000",
      "1≤ci,j≤2000001 \\le c_{i,j} \\le 2000001≤ci,j​≤200000 for each valid i,ji, ji,j",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (20 points):** N≤100N \\le 100N≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer NNN.\nNNN lines follow. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines contains an integer ∣Ai∣|A_i|∣Ai​∣ followed by a space and ∣Ai∣|A_i|∣Ai​∣ space-separated non-negative integers ci,1,ci,2,…,ci,∣Ai∣c_{i,1}, c_{i,2}, \\ldots, c_{i,|A_i|}ci,1​,ci,2​,…,ci,∣Ai​∣​.",
    "outputFormat": "Print a single line containing one integer ― the number of ways to choose (a1,a2,…,aN)(a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_N)(a1​,a2​,…,aN​), modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
